5. Learn to identify reusable distributed-system pattern
       This is directly related to the requirement you mentioned earlier about:
              breaking complex problems into manageable sub-problems and reusing solutions effectively.

Build a mental library of patterns.

              Traffic problem
                     → Load balancer
              
              Repeated expensive computation
                     → Cache
              
              Large dataset
                     → Partitioning/sharding
              
              Independent asynchronous work
                     → Queue/event streaming
              
              Slow downstream service
                     → Async processing
              
              Failure-prone dependency
                     → Timeout + retry + circuit breaker
              
              Duplicate requests
                     → Idempotency
              
              Database + event consistency
                     → Transactional outbox
              
              Independent service scaling
                     → Microservices
              
              Read-heavy workload
                     → Cache/read replicas
              
              High availability
                     → Replication
              
              Ordered processing
                     → Partition/key-based ordering
              
              Rate control
                     → Rate limiter

This becomes your architecture pattern library.


